+  `{ expiresAt: <ISO datetime with Z or offset> }`. It must be in the future (else 400); no
+  body or `{}` means the secret never expires. `expiresAt` belongs to the secret, so every
+  issue sets it: re-issuing without it **clears** it to `null`. The response and
+  `GET /devices/:id` show `expiresAt`. From the `expiresAt` instant on (inclusive) the
+  secret is refused by `verifyAccessKey`, with the same failure as a wrong secret.
